WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.270
In British labs, scientists
use live animals in research,

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.150
mainly mice, rats and fish.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.100
Since 1986, every project has needed
a licence from the government.

4
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.970
The aim is to understand disease and
develop new medicines and vaccines.

5
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:21.890
So could saving human lives ever
justify harming animals in a lab,

6
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.460
or growing organs in pigs?

7
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:29.000
In this mission, you'll meet the 3
Rs that guide research on animals:

8
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.090
replace, reduce, refine.

9
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.370
Then you'll weigh one
experiment on Bentham's scales,

10
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.790
and set it against Mill's rules.

11
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.390
Your mission: find out whether saving human
lives could ever justify harming animals.
